## R1 Reduction Test: Function with depends on

Tests that function-typed variables with a single unconditional rule
do NOT produce `match some(e) with | some r => r | _ => default` inside
the lambda body.

Before R1 reduction, the leaf function would be:
```
def ComputeTax_compute_leaf_0 (input : ComputeTax_Input) : Option (Money → Money) :=
  some (fun (x : Money) => match some ((multiply x input.rate)) with | some r => r | _ => default)
```

After R1 reduction, the leaf function becomes:
```
def ComputeTax_compute_leaf_0 (input : ComputeTax_Input) : Option (Money → Money) :=
  some (fun (x : Money) => (multiply x input.rate))
```

```catala
declaration scope ComputeTax:
  input rate content decimal
  output compute content money depends on x content money

scope ComputeTax:
  definition compute of x equals x * rate
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala Typecheck --check-invariants
┌─[RESULT]─
│ All invariant checks passed
└─
┌─[RESULT]─
│ Typechecking successful!
└─
```
